enchilada: GL display surfaces: 'b3a8' made as BGRA, cacheable surfaces kept off the GPU

With the OpenGL ES renderer on, CoreAnimation makes the display's surfaces 'b3a8'
(30RGBLE_8A_BiPlanar: 10-bit RGB in 32-bit pixels plus an 8-bit alpha plane; seen 1125x2436
bpe 4 bpr 4544, 2 planes). eagl.c's -attachImage takes only single-plane 'BGRA' (or no format)
with 4 bytes a pixel, so it said "not done", CA's framebuffer had a texture without storage as
its colour attachment, every glDrawElements was GL_INVALID_FRAMEBUFFER_OPERATION (0x506), no
target was ever drawn ("0 pictures copied out, 0 drawn in place") and the panel stayed black.
SweetSurface now makes such a surface as one plane of BGRA with the requested size and row
pitch, as HakiOS' kernel does (the panel is 8-bit sRGB anyway); IOSurface.framework reads
format and planes from the kernel, so CA, the GL layer and the framebuffer all see BGRA and
the existing BGRA attach and present paths take it. Unexpected geometry keeps 'b3a8' (the old
behaviour). Once BGRA, the surface also passes the zero-copy checks, but SURFACE_BO of a
cacheable surface gave the GPU memory nobody keeps coherent: the GPU does not snoop, boFlush()
needs an arena pa (surface BOs have none) and sweet_gpu_cache_sync() is only a barrier, so the
panel copy would read stale lines of GPU-written frames. SURFACE_BO now maps only uncached
(write-combined) surfaces; for the rest the client copies: eagl.c renders into its own texture
and glReadPixels it into the surface at the frame's end (0197 makes that readback cacheable).

--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetAdreno.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetAdreno.cpp
@@ -880,6 +880,22 @@
 		s->release();
 		return kIOReturnSuccess;
 	}
+	/*
+	 * 0198: the GPU does not snoop the CPU's caches, and nothing keeps a surface BO coherent:
+	 * boFlush() needs an arena pa (surface BOs have none) and sweet_gpu_cache_sync() is a barrier.
+	 * A cacheable surface (IOBufferMemoryDescriptor or client memory) shared with the GPU would
+	 * show stale lines both ways (the panel copy reading old frames, CPU-drawn pictures not yet
+	 * in DRAM). Only uncached ones (the panel) are mapped; the client copies the rest.
+	 */
+	if (s->mapCache != kIOMapWriteCombineCache) {
+		static uint32_t told;
+		if (told++ < 4) {
+			IOLog("SWEET GPU: surface %u (%ux%u fmt 0x%x) is cacheable: no GPU mapping, the client copies\n",
+			    s->id, s->width, s->height, s->pixelFormat);
+		}
+		s->release();
+		return kIOReturnUnsupported;
+	}
 	if (size == 0 || size > GEM_SIZE_MAX) {
 		s->release();
 		return kIOReturnBadArgument;
